 least one hour or until double in size. At the end of the rise, preheat the oven to 450 degrees.', 'Using a sharp knife or a serrated bread knife, gently make a few slits across the top of the dough. Brush or spritz the dough with water and bake for about 30 minutes or until the crust is a deep golden brown. Remove from the oven and cool on a wire rack.'], prep_time=190, cook_time=30, servings=12, cuisine_type='American', difficulty_level=None, image_url='https://www.budgetbytes.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/12/720baked.jpg', nutrition={'servingSize': '1 Serving', 'calories': '161.92 kcal', 'carbohydrateContent': '30.55 g', 'proteinContent': '5.21 g', 'fatContent': '2.43 g', 'fiberContent': '2.29 g', 'sodiumContent': '247.27 mg'}, macros=MacroNutrition(calories=161.92, protein=5.21, carbohydrates=30.55, fat=2.43, fiber=2.29, sugar=57.2, sodium=247.27, saturated_fat=12.399999999999999, cholesterol=None, monounsaturated_fat=None, polyunsaturated_fat=None), tags=['Bread,Dinner,Lunch', 'American'], dietary_restrictions=[], author='Beth Moncel', rating=4.64, provider=None)
